{
  "description": "WCAG 2.2 AA contrast of form themes: colour pairs with their contrast ratio, and themes with the pairings that fail and the nearest colours that pass. Run by backend/tests/app/services/test_theme_contrast.py (services/theme_contrast.py, the publish check theme_contrast) and webapp src/utils/theme-contrast-cases.test.ts (utils/color-contrast.ts, themeContrastGuard in utils/theme-contrast.ts), so the builder's guard and the server's publish check can't drift. 'ratio' to 6 decimals (null: a colour that is not hex, which fails every check); 'display' is the ratio as shown, one decimal rounded down. Text needs 4.5:1, controls 3:1. A theme's 'issues' are in the order text, answer, button, outlined, border, action, each at its lowest ratio; 'fix' holds only the keys that change (null when nothing fails); an image page can't be measured ('imageGround'). Every preset is listed and passes. An outlined button (buttonStyle 'outlined') is not white text on the button colour: its ink (the button colour where it reads at 4.5:1 on the page, else the questions' colour) is measured against the page colour (text 4.5:1) and against every page ground (its edge, 3:1), key 'outlined'; the white-on-button rule (key 'button') does not apply to it. 'keys': pairs of themes that must ('same': true) or must not ('same': false) produce the same contrast key, the key publishing compares to tell whether an older live form's colours changed (backend theme_contrast.contrast_key, webapp contrastKey): it holds the four colours (hex case ignored), whether buttons are outlined, and the ground the guard reads (an image with an address; both stops of a gradient; the white sheet of the margin pattern; else the plain page), so a re-saved or leftover background that shows no difference is no change. Keys are compared within a language, never across.",
